Standalone anchored tabs, double-click tab rename, and a divergence-only
anchor indicator.

- Adds an explicit per-tab "anchored" flag to TabUIHelper (persisted across
  sessions like the existing custom title / anchored URL) so a standalone
  (ungrouped, unpinned) tab can be anchored on its own. helium::IsAnchoredTab
  honours the flag, and the vertical tab strip lays such tabs out in the
  anchored region above the separator.
- Dragging a tab above the anchored separator anchors it; dragging it below
  un-anchors it. The decision is applied only on a completed drop (the
  TabDragTarget end-of-drag notification now carries a `completed` flag so a
  cancelled/reverted drag leaves anchored state untouched).
- Double-clicking an anchored tab opens the existing tab rename editor.
- The "/" anchor indicator is shown only once a tab has navigated away from its
  original anchored URL, acting as a "return to anchor" hint.

